1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,400
Your diaphragm suddenly yanks down,

2
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:04,040
air rushes into your lungs,

3
00:00:04,040 --> 00:00:06,580
and a split second later your vocal cords slam

4
00:00:06,580 --> 00:00:09,100
shut, making that hic sound.

5
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:11,680
It usually starts when your stomach stretches from eating

6
00:00:11,680 --> 00:00:13,940
too fast or drinking soda,

7
00:00:13,940 --> 00:00:16,700
irritating the nerves that control your breathing.

8
00:00:16,700 --> 00:00:19,160
You see, some scientists think hiccups are left over

9
00:00:19,160 --> 00:00:21,880
from our ancestors that lived in water because tadpoles

10
00:00:21,880 --> 00:00:24,080
use the same motion to push water over their

11
00:00:24,080 --> 00:00:27,320
gills. Another idea is that hiccups help babies burp

12
00:00:27,320 --> 00:00:28,220
out air while nursing.

13
00:00:28,220 --> 00:00:31,320
But one man hiccupped for 68 years straight,

14
00:00:31,320 --> 00:00:33,440
about 430 million times,

15
00:00:33,440 --> 00:00:35,540
and they finally stopped just a year before he

16
00:00:35,540 --> 00:00:36,200
died.
